الهدف: نعرف هل البيئة بتقدر تشغّل متصفح headless. الصق الدستور ثم البرومبت ده:
Build the smallest possible full-stack app that tests whether this environment can run a headless browser on the server. Build nothing else.
1. Add a server route GET /api/feasibility.
2. The route attempts the following steps in order and reports each step's REAL outcome (ok or failed plus the exact error message truncated to 500 chars): (a) install or load the 'playwright' package; (b) launch headless Chromium (retry once with the --no-sandbox argument only if the first launch fails, and report which variant worked); (c) open https://example.com, read the page title, take a JPEG screenshot 640 px wide, report its byte size; (d) install or load 'lighthouse' and 'chrome-launcher' and run one mobile Lighthouse performance audit on https://example.com, report the LCP value; (e) report the Node.js version, available memory, and whether outbound HTTPS works.
3. One page calls the route and shows the JSON result readably.
4. Never fake a success. If a step fails, show the exact error. Use a 120 second overall timeout and no endless retries.
At the end, list what you could not verify.
