5. المرحلة 1 — الواجهة والشات والتقرير على بيانات تجريبية (في AI Studio)
الصق الدستور ثم العقد ثم البرومبت ده:
STAGE 1: Build the complete app experience (UI + server) running on MOCK scan data that conforms exactly to the CONTRACT. Do not implement real scanning.

ARCHITECTURE
- Full-stack web app: React frontend, Node.js server. Keep the structure simple and typed.
- Environment variables (validated with Zod at startup, with defaults): SCAN_MODE (mock|live, default mock), WORKER_URL, WORKER_API_KEY, GEMINI_MODEL (use the platform's recommended default model; the model name may appear in exactly one default constant), AI_ENABLED (default true), FREE_SCANS_HARD_DISABLED (default false).
- Server modules: ScanProvider interface (start(request) returns an async stream of the CONTRACT events) with MockProvider (implemented) and LiveProvider (a stub that throws LIVE_NOT_CONFIGURED with a clear message; do not implement it), explainService, repairPromptBuilder, an in-memory scan store, routes.
- Routes: POST /api/scans (validate input, create scan, run provider in background, return scanId); GET /api/scans/:scanId (current stage states, pages count, status, and the final ScanResult when done); POST /api/scans/:scanId/explain; GET /api/quota (stub returning limit, remaining, resetAt).
- Use unguessable scan ids (random, at least 128 bits).

MOCK DATA
- MockProvider emits stage events with realistic delays (0.8 to 2 seconds per stage), page events, then done. The UI must render only real event state. No timers that fake progress percentages.
- The final ScanResult has: 4 pages, 7 findings covering all severities and all five kinds (confirmed_defect, suspected_issue, unverified_behavior, recommendation, measurement), 2 Lighthouse runs, and 1 limitation. Include one tiny generated placeholder screenshot (data URL under 5 KB, no external images).
- While SCAN_MODE=mock, show a persistent banner on every screen: «نسخة تجريبية — النتايج دي عينة مش فحص حقيقي».

URL INPUT (server-side validation with Zod)
- http or https only, no embedded credentials, max 2048 chars, hostname must contain a dot, reject IP literals and localhost. Normalize: trim, lowercase host, drop the fragment. Use the 'tldts' package for the registrable domain. (Full SSRF protection lives in the scanner; this is a first filter only.)

MADAM AFAF CHAT (deterministic script, no LLM needed)
- Greeting, then ask for the URL. Optional question 1: site purpose, as clickable chips: موقع شركة / متجر إلكتروني / صفحة هبوط / موقع حجز أو خدمات / مش متأكد، افحصيه وخلاص. Optional question 2: the most important user journey, free text, with a skip chip «ابدأ الفحص دلوقتي».
- One short question at a time. Chips plus free text. Every question skippable. Never ask for information already provided.
- Before starting, a required checkbox: «أنا صاحب الموقع ده أو مفوّض بفحصه». The start button stays disabled until the URL is valid and the box is checked.

PROGRESS SCREEN
- Show the five stages (فحص الرابط، اكتشاف الصفحات المهمة، اختبار التفاعل، مراجعة الأداء وSEO، تجهيز التقرير) with real state from events, the current stage, and the count of inspected pages. No fake percentages.

REPORT SCREEN
- Header: domain, time, «اتفحص X صفحات من حد أقصى Y», and the limitations list.
- No overall website score anywhere.
- Show the top 3 to 5 findings first: sort by severity (critical, high, medium, low, improvement), then confidence (confirmed, likely, unverified).
- Arabic labels for kinds: مشكلة مؤكدة / مشكلة محتملة / سلوك لم يتم التحقق منه / توصية / قياس.
- Finding card: severity badge, confidence badge, kind, affected page, plain Arabic explanation, reproduction steps, evidence (screenshot with a lightbox; text evidence collapsed), recommended fix, a «انسخ برومبت الإصلاح» button, and expandable technical details (ruleId, source, observed, expected).
- Lighthouse section: metrics labeled «قياس معملي (Lab) — مش بالضرورة تجربة زوارك الفعلية».
- A master repair prompt box with a copy button and the confirmation «اتنسخ ✓», plus one prompt per finding.
- Accessibility: keyboard operable, visible focus, Arabic ARIA labels, AA contrast, respect prefers-reduced-motion. Correct RTL using logical CSS properties. Use a readable Arabic font such as Cairo or Tajawal.

EXPLANATIONS (explainService)
- One Gemini call per scan covering at most 8 top findings. System instruction contains the style guide below. Findings go inside a delimited block <finding_data>...</finding_data> marked as untrusted data. Request structured JSON output (per finding: explanationAr, whyItMattersAr, each at most 60 words) and validate it with Zod. Retry once if malformed. Bound max output tokens.
- The model must not change severity, confidence, or kind, and must not add or remove findings. Anything beyond the schema is discarded.
- On any failure, or if AI_ENABLED=false, use deterministic Arabic fallback templates keyed by ruleId (write templates for every ruleId in the mock data plus one generic fallback) and show the small note «الشرح ده جاهز مش مولّد بالـ AI».

STYLE GUIDE (Madam Afaf)
- Friendly, meticulous, direct, respectful Egyptian Arabic. Plain words, no heavy slang, no scare tactics, at most one emoji per message.
- Certainty wording follows confidence: confirmed = «لقينا», likely = «غالبًا», unverified = «مش متأكدين».
- Examples to imitate:
  • Broken link: «الرابط ده بيودّي على صفحة مش موجودة (404). الزائر هيشوف رسالة خطأ بدل المحتوى. اتأكد من العنوان أو شيل الرابط.»
  • Mobile overflow: «على الموبايل الصفحة بتعدّي عرض الشاشة، فالزائر هيضطر يسحب يمين وشمال. غالبًا في صورة أو جدول عرضه أكبر من الشاشة.»
  • Missing title: «الصفحة من غير عنوان، وده بيأثر على ظهورها في جوجل وعلى اسم التبويبة في المتصفح.»
  • Slow LCP: «أكبر عنصر في الصفحة بياخد وقت طويل لحد ما يظهر في القياس ده. ممكن تكون صورة تقيلة. القياس معملي وممكن يختلف عن تجربة زوارك.»
  • Suspected: «الزرار ده ماعملش تغيير واضح لما ضغطنا عليه، بس مش متأكدين إنه عيب. محتاج حد يجرّبه بإيده.»
  • Recommendation: «مش عيب، بس لو ضفت وصف للصور هتبقى الصفحة أوضح لقارئ الشاشة ولجوجل.»

REPAIR PROMPT BUILDER (pure deterministic function, no LLM)
- Output an English prompt (universal for any AI coding tool or human developer) with: website purpose if given; the prioritized findings (confirmed first), each with affected URLs, reproduction steps, observed behavior, expected behavior only when present, evidence summary, and recommended change; then fixed instructions: inspect the existing implementation before editing, make minimal targeted changes, preserve the existing framework, design system, routes, and unrelated functionality, add no unnecessary dependencies or redesigns, test the fix and check for regressions, and report changed files and unresolved limitations. Never name a specific builder tool. Never include more than the top 10 findings in the master prompt.
- Add Vitest unit tests for the builder and the URL normalizer. If you cannot run tests in this environment, say so.

ACCEPTANCE (you must verify and report each)
1. A full mock scan runs from the chat to the report with the progress driven by events. 2. The checkbox gate and URL validation work. 3. All five kinds are displayed correctly in Arabic. 4. No overall score is shown. 5. Copy buttons work and show the confirmation. 6. With AI_ENABLED=false the fallback explanations appear. 7. The mock banner shows on every screen. 8. No API key or model secret is present in client code.
6. المرحلة 2 — محرك الفحص (في أداة برمجة عندها shell)
استخدم أداة برمجة تقدر تشغّل أوامر وتختبر (Claude Code أو Codex CLI أو Gemini CLI أو غيرها)، في مشروع منفصل اسمه afaf-scanner. الصق الدستور ثم العقد ثم البرومبت. قبل النشر جهّز: صفحة تعريف بالأداة فيها طريقة طلب عدم الفحص (تتحط في USER_AGENT_CONTACT_URL)، ومفتاح WORKER_API_KEY عشوائي طويل (32 حرف أو أكتر).
STAGE 2: Build the scanner service 'afaf-scanner' as a standalone repository.

STACK
- TypeScript on the current Node.js LTS that the installed Playwright and Lighthouse versions support (check their engines fields). Fastify, Playwright (Chromium), Lighthouse (programmatic API), tldts, Zod, Vitest, Docker. Pin all versions. No Redis, no BullMQ, no database.

API
- GET /healthz returns 200 when the process is ready.
- POST /v1/scan accepts a ScanRequest (validate with Zod), requires the header Authorization: Bearer <WORKER_API_KEY> (constant-time comparison), and answers with text/event-stream using the CONTRACT events. One request equals one scan. No state survives after the response ends.
- Process-wide concurrency is 1. If busy, answer HTTP 429 with JSON body {code:'busy'}.
- Global timeout SCAN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (default 180). On timeout finish with status 'partial' if the homepage was inspected, else 'failed', and add a limitation.
- On client disconnect abort the scan and release every browser resource.

CONFIG (Zod, from env, with defaults)
WORKER_API_KEY (required), PORT, STANDARD_MAX_PAGES=10, LIGHTHOUSE_MAX_PAGES=3, PER_PAGE_TIMEOUT_MS=20000, MAX_REDIRECTS=5, MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES=5000000, SCAN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180, MAX_REQUESTS_PER_SCAN=400, MIN_DELAY_BETWEEN_PAGES_MS=500, USER_AGENT_CONTACT_URL, ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS_FOR_TESTS (default false; if true while NODE_ENV is not 'test', the process must refuse to start).

SSRF PROTECTION (most important; implement and test this first)
1. URL gate: http or https only; no credentials; ports other than 80 and 443 rejected by default; localhost rejected; IP-literal hosts allowed only if they pass the IP rule.
2. IP rule: reject loopback, private (RFC1918), link-local (including 169.254.169.254), CGNAT (100.64.0.0/10), unspecified, multicast, reserved, and the IPv6 equivalents (::1, fc00::/7, fe80::/10). IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses are checked as IPv4. Reject the host metadata.google.internal and any name resolving to a rejected address.
3. Resolve DNS yourself and validate EVERY resolved address.
4. Connection-time enforcement against DNS rebinding: run an in-process forward proxy (HTTP CONNECT and plain HTTP) bound to 127.0.0.1 on a random port. Launch Chromium with --proxy-server pointing at it. The proxy resolves the target, validates all addresses, and connects to the validated IP itself, so the browser can never reach an address that was not validated at connect time. The proxy also enforces MAX_REQUESTS_PER_SCAN and response byte limits. ALL Playwright and Lighthouse traffic goes through it.
5. Redirects: every hop is re-validated (the proxy does this); cap at MAX_REDIRECTS. Meta-refresh and JavaScript redirects: re-validate the destination before following. Pop-ups and new windows are closed. Frames pointing outside the allowed origin are not inspected.
6. Defense in depth: the README must state that the deployment must ALSO block egress to private ranges and the cloud metadata address at the network level, and that the container carries no cloud credentials.

BROWSER HYGIENE
Fresh browser context per scan: service workers blocked, downloads disabled, permissions denied, no persisted storage, JavaScript dialogs auto-dismissed, ignoreHTTPSErrors false. Close page, context, and browser in finally blocks on success, error, timeout, and abort. Never submit forms. Never click elements whose accessible name or attributes suggest purchase, payment, delete, logout, send, or publish.

POLITENESS
User-Agent: 'AfafScanner/1.0 (+<USER_AGENT_CONTACT_URL>)'. Respect robots.txt (fetch with size and time limits; if a path is disallowed, skip it and add a limitation). Keep a minimum delay between page loads. No bot-protection bypass: if a response looks like a challenge page (403, 429, or 503 with challenge markers), stop inspecting that site and report a limitation (status 'blocked' if nothing could be inspected).

DISCOVERY AND PAGE COUNTING
- Normalize URLs: lowercase host, strip fragment and default ports, remove tracking params (utm_*, fbclid, gclid, msclkid, mc_cid, mc_eid, ref, ref_src, igshid), sort the remaining params.
- Registrable domain via tldts. Stay on the canonical host of that domain (follow one validated redirect between www and apex). Never crawl other hosts.
- Breadth-first from the homepage. Priority: homepage, primary navigation targets, contact and about pages, header and footer links, then the rest. Dedupe by normalized URL and rel=canonical. Treat filter, sort, pagination, and session params (sort, order, filter*, page, p, sessionid, variant, color, size, q, search) as the same page unless the canonical URL differs.
- Hard cap: STANDARD_MAX_PAGES unique meaningful pages, enforced inside the crawler loop itself. At the cap, stop discovery and add a limitation stating how many discovered links were not inspected. Never follow infinite scroll or pagination chains.
- Counters: uniquePagesInspected and interactionStatesTested (always 0 in this stage).
- Site type in this stage: siteProfile type 'unknown' with empty signals. E-commerce handling is Stage 4.

CHECKS (each yields a Finding with the ruleId, evidence, and reproduction steps; dedupe by ruleId plus normalized target and count occurrences)
R001 page_unreachable: homepage non-2xx, DNS failure, TLS failure, or timeout -> critical, confirmed, confirmed_defect. Other pages -> high.
R002 broken_internal_link: same-domain target returns 4xx or 5xx (HEAD then GET fallback, bounded) -> high if in the header or primary nav, else medium; confirmed.
R003 empty_link: anchor with missing, empty, or '#'-only href and no evidence of a JS handler -> low, likely.
R004 broken_image: visible image that is complete with naturalWidth 0 -> medium if above the fold, else low; confirmed.
R005 horizontal_overflow_mobile: at a 390x844 viewport, document scrollWidth exceeds clientWidth by more than 1 px after load plus a bounded settle -> medium, confirmed; include a screenshot and the selector of the widest offending element when identifiable.
R006 missing_viewport_meta -> medium, confirmed.
R007 missing_title: missing or empty title -> medium, confirmed (category seo).
R008 missing_meta_description -> improvement, confirmed, kind recommendation.
R009 console_exception: uncaught exceptions only (pageerror), ignoring a configurable list of analytics, ads, and tag-manager domains and cancelled requests -> low, likely. Never report console.log or plain warnings.
R010 failed_request_first_party: first-party requests failing with 5xx or network errors -> low, likely. Third-party request failures are never reported as defects.
R011 form_input_unlabeled: form control without an accessible label (aria-label, aria-labelledby, label for, or a wrapping label) -> low, confirmed (category accessibility).
R012 images_missing_alt: img without an alt attribute -> improvement, recommendation.
R013 lighthouse measurements: kind 'measurement' only for mobile LCP above 4000 ms, CLS above 0.25, TBT above 600 ms; severity at most 'medium'. Failed Lighthouse SEO audits become 'recommendation'.
Use only these rules in Stage 2. Do not invent others. No LLM is involved in this service.

SCREENSHOTS
At most 4 per scan, JPEG quality about 60, 640 px wide, each at most 80 KB (lower the quality or crop if larger). Only for R001, R004, R005.

LIGHTHOUSE
Run mobile Lighthouse on the homepage and up to LIGHTHOUSE_MAX_PAGES minus 1 other important pages, one at a time, using a separate Chromium instance launched through the same validating proxy and controlled through its remote debugging port. Extract FCP, LCP, CLS, TBT, Speed Index, and the performance and seo category scores (real Lighthouse lab values), plus failed audits. If Lighthouse fails for a page, record a limitation and continue. Label everything as lab measurement.

STREAMING STAGES (real state only)
url_check, discovery, interaction (state 'skipped' with detail 'not enabled in this version'), lighthouse, report. Emit page events as pages are inspected. Always finish with exactly one 'done' or 'error' event.

